ake County, UT Property Tax Guide: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Salt Lake County, UT Property Tax Guide sale</li><li>Turn the Salt Lake County, UT Property Tax Guide offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling in Salt Lake County? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy Salt Lake County houses as-is and reply with a written cash offer.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Salt Lake County, Utah property tax involves the county assessment office and the county treasurer.</strong></p><h2>Who to contact in Salt Lake County</h2><ul><li><a href='https://slco.org/treasurer/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Salt Lake County Treasurer</a></li><li><a href='https://slco.org/assessor/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Salt Lake County Assessor</a> handles assessment and appeals.</li></ul><h2>What we confirmed on official pages</h2><ul><li>Assessor appraises all County property as of January 1; Assessor completes assessment roll by May 22</li><li>Greenbelt (Farmland Assessment Act) applications due May 1 to the County Assessor</li><li>November 30: last day to pay current-year property taxes without penalty; extended to next business day if weekend/holiday</li><li>Dec 1 unpaid taxes become delinquent; penalty greater of 2.5% or $10 per parcel, reduced to greater of 1% or $10 if paid by Jan 31</li><li>After Jan 31, penalty becomes 2.5% (min $10) plus statutory interest retroactive to Jan 1</li><li>Tax sale: redemption period expires March 15 of the 5th year after delinquency; Auditor holds tax sale in late May</li></ul><h2>Tax rate</h2><p> Utah bills combine county, municipal and school district levies.</p><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Salt Lake County?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Salt Lake County houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Salt Lake County by the numbers</h2><p>Salt Lake County ranks 1 of 10 Utah counties in this guide by population, at about 1,184,689 people in 440,166 housing units (Census Bureau, 2019-2023). At $484,500, the median home value sits 13% above the Utah county median for this guide. The Utah county median income is $90,870, and Salt Lake County reports $94,658. Owner-occupancy is 67%, so renters hold about 33% of occupied homes.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/utah-property-tax-guide/'>Utah Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/utah-homestead-exemption/'>Utah Homestead Exemption Guide</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><di